# Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-First Config)

This project uses Tailwind v4 with CSS-first configuration. There is NO `tailwind.config.js`.

## Configuration Location

All theme config lives in `src/styles/globals.css`:
- `@import "tailwindcss"` loads the framework
- `@plugin 'tailwindcss-animate'` loads the animation plugin
- `@theme { ... }` defines design tokens (colors, radii, animations)
- `@utility` defines custom utilities (like `container`)
- `@layer base` defines CSS custom properties for light/dark themes

## Theme Tokens

Colors use HSL CSS custom properties with the pattern:
```css
--color-primary: hsl(var(--primary));
```

Where `--primary` is defined in `:root` (light) and `.dark` (dark mode).

## Adding New Theme Values

Add to the `@theme` block in globals.css, NOT a config file:
```css
@theme {
  --color-my-new: hsl(var(--my-new));
}
```

Then define the HSL value in the `:root` and `.dark` layers.

## PostCSS

`postcss.config.js` only loads `@tailwindcss/postcss`. No autoprefixer needed (it's built in).

## Dark Mode

Uses class strategy via `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))`. Currently forced to light theme via ThemeProvider.
